OL,3,GNEWSAWorld War Two refugee committee
OL,4,Arecords go online
OL,5,
OL,6,FRecords of people who fled from Nazi
OL,7,Fpersecution in World War Two to a part
OL,8,Fof Surrey have now been made accessible
OL,9,Fonline for the first time.
OL,11,FThe records are from the papers of the
OL,12,FDorking and District Refugee Committee
OL,13,F` a group of volunteers who were able
OL,14,Fto find housing, work and medical care
OL,15,Ffor refugees arriving in the Surrey
OL,16,Ftown between 1938 and 1949.
OL,18,FUntil now, the records have only
OL,19,Fexisted in paper form at the Dorking
OL,20,FMuseum, but have now moved to a digital
OL,21,Fform after it worked with the
OL,22,FUniversity of Surrey.
